==Strategy==
Stalling at the start to build up money may be a good idea since the initial peon waves are not too strong, although the first Gory Dark might catch players off guard.

Bring at least 3 meatshields, as Gory Dark and Shadow Boxer K are very aggressive pushers and tough enemies to handle for early-game players. Stackable midrangers such as [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] and [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] can juggle the enemies while main damage units like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] pick them off. Do note that Bahamut can miss its attacks thanks to the high knockback count of Dark enemies.

Due to the high dps of the enemy units, melee Cats (e.g. [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Whale Cat]]) are not recommended since they will get shredded before dealing much damage. However, they can serve as beefier meatshields in a pinch.

If one owns [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ring Girl Cat]], this stage will be trivial as long as you meatshield well enough.

